From 12e5b8d6c86e6d623656e5c188c65b55548ecea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:34:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 3106 (speed), again: the server finds the weather, and every
 call reads it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

0283 regressed (the tester's 58065): the server's web search ran, but
the weather section went into the first turn's prompt only. The final
writer (and any later round) never saw it and wrote „ცოცხლად ვერ
ვამოწმებ", which in turn woke the weather guard's extra rounds: 25-34 s
and no weather. Reverted by 0289.

This is 0283 again with the cause removed: the section is part of the
run's whole system prompt (runToolLoop's systemPrompt is now built from
the prompt before the run plus the weather found), so the first turn,
every later round and the final writer all read the same results. A
failed or empty server search still falls back to the forced web_search.
No new model-facing text: the opening-search section is the one goals use.

Ships after 0289 (built on it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
